#
# Declarative structural assertions for the learning slice — the slice-resident
# test-DSL twin of the MUST / MUST-NOT invariants formerly hand-written in
# tests/test_learning.py. Authored as gmeow: ontology data so the same annotation
# discipline and the native Rust harness (crates/slicetest) drive the test,
# not ad-hoc Python. Each assertion runs as a SPARQL ASK over the slice module
# graph (gmeow:scopeModule); every `must` ASK anchors on a concrete term IRI.
#
# NAMESPACE: the learning module is migrated — its value classes are
# typed with the canonical logic meta-vocabulary (logic:Event, logic:AbstractIndividualType,
# logic:Kind, logic:Relator, logic:QualityValue). These cells mirror the module's
# CURRENT logic: shape.
#
# The slice's SHACL invariants (gmeow:TeachingShape — teacher ≠ learner, learner
# must be an Agent) are migrated separately to tests/example-conformance.ttl. The
# annotation-completeness test (test_every_declared_term_is_annotated) is subsumed
# by the global `make validate` gate via TWO guardians — SHACL GmeowClassShape /
# GmeowPropertyShape for the classes/properties AND the Rust structural_lint
# vocabulary-individual sweep for the 6 LearningEventType value individuals.
# Verified 2026-06-23 by break-and-revert: deleting gmeow:learningSkillAcquisition's
# rdfs:label (a value-vocab INDIVIDUAL) emitted "error individual … is missing
# rdfs:label" (the Rust guardian) and deleting gmeow:LearningEvent's rdfs:label
# (a CLASS) emitted "error class … is missing rdfs:label" (the SHACL guardian);
# both reverted. That pytest function is therefore deleted rather than migrated.
#

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/learning/tests/> .

# --- 1. LearningEvent reparents MentalProcess (MUST) -------------------------
ex:saLearningEventReparentsMentalProcess a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:LearningEvent a owl:Class , logic:Event ;
        rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:MentalProcess .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:LearningEvent is the OCCURRENT that transitions an agent's knowledge state: it MUST be an owl:Class, a logic:Event, and a subClassOf gmeow:MentalProcess (the reparenting hook the mentation slice reserves), exactly as the sibling gmeow:InferenceProcess." .

# --- 2. processLearning marker rides instances, not the class (MUST-NOT) -------
ex:saProcessLearningMarkerRidesInstances a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    { gmeow:processLearning a gmeow:MentalProcessType . }
    UNION
    { gmeow:LearningEvent gmeow:mentalProcessType ?x . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Two invariants (P6 / P9): gmeow:processLearning is declared ONCE on the mentation spine — the learning module references but never redeclares it, so it carries NO gmeow:MentalProcessType typing here; and the marker rides each LearningEvent INSTANCE, never the CLASS (no overtyping), so gmeow:LearningEvent itself MUST NOT carry a gmeow:mentalProcessType." .

# --- 3. LearningEventType is a value-vocab class (MUST) ----------------------
ex:saLearningEventTypeIsAbstractIndividualType a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:LearningEventType a owl:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ;
        rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:LearningEventType is the variety value vocabulary: it MUST be an owl:Class, a logic:AbstractIndividualType, and a subClassOf logic:QualityValue — the value-vocab genus." .

# --- 4a. The six LearningEventType individuals are seeded (MUST) -------------
ex:saLearningEventTypeIndividualsSeeded a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:learningConceptFormation a gmeow:LearningEventType .
    gmeow:learningSkillAcquisition a gmeow:LearningEventType .
    gmeow:learningBeingTaught      a gmeow:LearningEventType .
    gmeow:learningConsolidation    a gmeow:LearningEventType .
    gmeow:learningTransfer         a gmeow:LearningEventType .
    gmeow:learningUnlearning       a gmeow:LearningEventType .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The six learning-event-type values MUST be individuals of gmeow:LearningEventType — an open value vocabulary." .

# --- 4b. Those individuals are NOT subclasses of LearningEvent (MUST-NOT) -----
ex:saLearningEventTypeIndividualsNotSubclasses a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    VALUES ?i {
        gmeow:learningConceptFormation gmeow:learningSkillAcquisition
        gmeow:learningBeingTaught gmeow:learningConsolidation
        gmeow:learningTransfer gmeow:learningUnlearning
    }
    ?i rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:LearningEvent .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Value-vocab discipline (P9): NO LearningEventType value individual is a subClassOf gmeow:LearningEvent — members are individuals, never subclasses." .

# --- 5a. learningType is a LearningEvent→LearningEventType ObjectProperty (MUST)
ex:saLearningTypeProperty a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:learningType a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain gmeow:LearningEvent ;
        rdfs:range gmeow:LearningEventType .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:learningType carries the variety: it MUST be an owl:ObjectProperty from gmeow:LearningEvent to gmeow:LearningEventType." .

# --- 5b. learningType is NOT functional (MUST-NOT) ---------------------------
ex:saLearningTypeNotFunctional a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK { ?rec logic:characterizes gmeow:learningType ; logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty . }""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:learningType MUST NOT be functional — several varieties may co-apply to one event." .

# --- 6a. provenance / trajectory / product properties + domains (MUST) -------
ex:saProvenanceTrajectoryProductProperties a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:subjectTaught a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:Teaching .
    gmeow:learnedFrom   a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:LearningEvent .
    gmeow:fromLevel     a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:LearningEvent .
    gmeow:toLevel       a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:LearningEvent .
    gmeow:produces      a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:LearningEvent .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The provenance/trajectory/product edges MUST be owl:ObjectProperty with the right domains: gmeow:subjectTaught on gmeow:Teaching; gmeow:learnedFrom / gmeow:fromLevel / gmeow:toLevel / gmeow:produces on gmeow:LearningEvent." .

# --- 6b. Those 5 properties keep an OPEN range and are non-functional (MUST-NOT)
ex:saProvenanceTrajectoryProductOpenRangeNotFunctional a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    VALUES ?p { gmeow:subjectTaught gmeow:learnedFrom gmeow:fromLevel gmeow:toLevel gmeow:produces }
    { ?p rdfs:range ?r . }
    UNION
    { ?rec logic:characterizes ?p ; logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "OPEN-range (P13): none of gmeow:subjectTaught / gmeow:learnedFrom / gmeow:fromLevel / gmeow:toLevel / gmeow:produces MUST assert an rdfs:range (the targets are retired gmeow:Source or not-yet-built gmeow:Concept) and none MUST be functional." .

# --- 7a. Teaching is a mediating Relator; teacher + learner ObjectProperties (MUST)
ex:saTeachingIsMediatingRelator a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:Teaching a owl:Class , logic:Kind ;
        rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:teacher a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain gmeow:Teaching ;
        rdfs:range gmeow:Agent .
    gmeow:learner a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain gmeow:Teaching ;
        rdfs:range gmeow:Agent .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:Teaching is the reified mediating relator: it MUST be an owl:Class, a logic:Kind, and a subClassOf logic:Relator; gmeow:teacher MUST be an owl:ObjectProperty with domain gmeow:Teaching and range gmeow:Agent; gmeow:learner MUST be an owl:ObjectProperty with domain gmeow:Teaching and range gmeow:Agent." .

# --- 7a'. learner is NOT functional (MUST-NOT) ------------------------------
ex:saLearnerNotFunctional a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
ASK { ?rec logic:characterizes gmeow:learner ; logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty . }""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:learner MUST NOT be functional — several learners may be taught together in one Teaching." .

# --- 7b. The EL someValuesFrom mediation restrictions on teacher + learner (MUST)
ex:saTeachingELRestrictions a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:Teaching rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
        owl:onProperty gmeow:teacher ; owl:someValuesFrom gmeow:Agent ] .
    gmeow:Teaching rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
        owl:onProperty gmeow:learner ; owl:someValuesFrom gmeow:Agent ] .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The EL relator-mediation restrictions MUST be present: gmeow:Teaching is an rdfs:subClassOf an owl:Restriction someValuesFrom gmeow:Agent on gmeow:teacher AND another on gmeow:learner (the blank-node existential walk this assertion performs)." .

# --- 8. No forgetting / truth bit; remembers not redeclared (MUST-NOT) -------
ex:saNoForgettingOrTruthBit a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    VALUES ?t {
        gmeow:forgets gmeow:forgotten gmeow:isLearned
        gmeow:unlearns gmeow:isTaught gmeow:remembers
    }
    { ?t ?p ?o . } UNION { ?s ?t ?o . } UNION { ?s ?p ?t . }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Forgetting is suppression, referenced not duplicated (P6): none of gmeow:forgets / gmeow:forgotten / gmeow:isLearned / gmeow:unlearns / gmeow:isTaught MUST appear in ANY triple position, and the slice MUST NOT redeclare the cognition slice's gmeow:remembers." .
